550
00:40:11.000 --> 00:40:14.000
But that crown would mean
she was a princess,

551
00:40:14.000 --> 00:40:17.000
and everybody loves a princess!

552
00:40:17.000 --> 00:40:20.000
So the wolf sent the piggies
to get that crown.

553
00:40:21.000 --> 00:40:24.000
But the little pigs
weren't up to the challenge.

554
00:40:24.000 --> 00:40:26.000
They failed their mission.

555
00:40:26.000 --> 00:40:33.000
So the wolf huffed and puffed,
and she blew them off the face of the earth!

556
00:40:34.000 --> 00:40:36.000
Yo, po, po!

557
00:40:39.000 --> 00:40:41.000
The end.

558
00:40:44.000 --> 00:40:48.000
Good luck getting
that crown tomorrow, little piggies.

559
00:40:48.000 --> 00:40:52.000
I know you won't disappoint me.

560
00:40:52.000 --> 00:40:54.000
Um.

561
00:41:07.000 --> 00:41:08.000
Okay.

562
00:41:08.000 --> 00:41:11.000
...Scarlet.

563
00:41:11.000 --> 00:41:12.000
Which way is the loo, please?
Hmm.

564
00:41:12.000 --> 00:41:15.000
Oh, thank you.
Ah.

565
00:41:16.000 --> 00:41:18.000
Bello.

566
00:41:18.000 --> 00:41:19.000
- Uh...
- ...please.

567
00:41:19.000 --> 00:41:24.000
You're not allowed in without an adult.
Scram, hooligans!

568
00:41:24.000 --> 00:41:25.000
Oh.

569
00:41:25.000 --> 00:41:29.000
Uh, mm.

570
00:41:32.000 --> 00:41:34.000
Ooh...

571
00:41:34.000 --> 00:41:36.000
Oh, la...

572
00:41:36.000 --> 00:41:38.000
Stuart...

573
00:41:42.000 --> 00:41:44.000
How many tickets, please?

574
00:41:45.000 --> 00:41:50.000
...please.

575
00:41:56.000 --> 00:41:57.000
Enjoy yourself, love.

576
00:41:57.000 --> 00:41:59.000
Thank you!

577
00:42:01.000 --> 00:42:04.000
It was nowhere near Hyde Park!

578
00:42:04.000 --> 00:42:06.000
Bob's your uncle.

579
00:42:06.000 --> 00:42:07.000
Huh, hmm.

580
00:42:07.000 --> 00:42:10.000
Okay.

581
00:42:16.000 --> 00:42:17.000
Okay.

582
00:42:17.000 --> 00:42:20.000
Huh? Ah!

583
00:42:21.000 --> 00:42:23.000
He-hey.

584
00:42:23.000 --> 00:42:24.000
Okay.

585
00:42:24.000 --> 00:42:25.000
Hey!

586
00:42:25.000 --> 00:42:28.000
What are you doing here?

587
00:42:29.000 --> 00:42:33.000
This is a restricted area!
Hands in the air!

588
00:42:33.000 --> 00:42:35.000
No...

589
00:42:40.000 --> 00:42:42.000
Stop that!

590
00:42:44.000 --> 00:42:47.000
Get back.

591
00:43:07.000 --> 00:43:09.000
Yay!

592
00:43:11.000 --> 00:43:14.000
Ah!

593
00:43:21.000 --> 00:43:23.000
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

594
00:43:23.000 --> 00:43:26.000
Bob, Stuart...

595
00:44:03.000 --> 00:44:05.000
So...

596
00:44:05.000 --> 00:44:09.000
So, you came for
the Queen's crown, did you?

597
00:44:09.000 --> 00:44:12.000
Well, you're gonna
have to get through me!

598
00:44:12.000 --> 00:44:16.000
The Keeper of the Crown!

599
00:44:19.000 --> 00:44:21.000
Ow! Hey!

600
00:44:21.000 --> 00:44:24.000
You think it's
funny to mock the elderly, do you?

601
00:44:24.000 --> 00:44:26.000
Uh...

602
00:44:26.000 --> 00:44:28.000
I've been up here for decades,

603
00:44:28.000 --> 00:44:30.000
just waiting for someone to try

604
00:44:30.000 --> 00:44:33.000
and steal the Queen's treasure!

605
00:44:34.000 --> 00:44:36.000
Okay.

606
00:44:37.000 --> 00:44:41.000
What are you saying?
Never mind, don't care!

607
00:44:44.000 --> 00:44:46.000
Oh, no!

608
00:44:46.000 --> 00:44:49.000
Oh, no, you don't!

609
00:44:50.000 --> 00:44:52.000
Oh, flippin' heck!

610
00:44:54.000 --> 00:44:56.000
What's goin' on?

611
00:45:01.000 --> 00:45:02.000
Bob...

612
00:45:02.000 --> 00:45:06.000
Eh... Hmm.
Wow.

613
00:45:33.000 --> 00:45:36.000
Hello!

614
00:45:40.000 --> 00:45:43.000
Huh?

615
00:45:55.000 --> 00:45:57.000
Hello!

616
00:45:57.000 --> 00:45:58.000
Stone the crows!

617
00:45:58.000 --> 00:45:59.000
Stop him, lads!
Wait!

618
00:45:59.000 --> 00:46:01.000
Go for the legs!

619
00:46:05.000 --> 00:46:07.000
Gordon Bennett!

620
00:46:07.000 --> 00:46:09.000
Kevin!

621
00:46:14.000 --> 00:46:16.000
The Queen's
been kidnapped, Sarge!

622
00:46:16.000 --> 00:46:18.000
Blimey!

623
00:46:23.000 --> 00:46:24.000
Hyah! Hyah!

624
00:46:24.000 --> 00:46:26.000
Ooh!

625
00:46:33.000 --> 00:46:35.000
Ha! Boo-ya!

626
00:46:40.000 --> 00:46:42.000
Huh. Hyah! Hyah!

627
00:46:42.000 --> 00:46:44.000
What's going on?
Bello!

628
00:46:44.000 --> 00:46:46.000
Oh, my goodness!

629
00:46:46.000 --> 00:46:48.000
- Whoa!
- Ha-ha!

630
00:46:48.000 --> 00:46:50.000
No!

631
00:46:50.000 --> 00:46:56.000
Gentlemen do not
steal ladies' crowns!

632
00:46:56.000 --> 00:46:58.000
Huh? Hmm?

633
00:47:06.000 --> 00:47:08.000
Huh?

634
00:47:12.000 --> 00:47:14.000
Oh, no, no, no, no, no!

635
00:47:18.000 --> 00:47:20.000
Oh, dear!

636
00:47:26.000 --> 00:47:28.000
Ah! Ahhh!

637
00:47:32.000 --> 00:47:34.000
Yeah!

638
00:47:34.000 --> 00:47:37.000
You scoundrel!
After them! Uh-oh.

639
00:47:40.000 --> 00:47:43.000
Stop the blighter!

640
00:47:43.000 --> 00:47:46.000
Go on, grab him!

641
00:47:46.000 --> 00:47:48.000
Huh?

642
00:47:53.000 --> 00:47:55.000
Huh? Oh.

643
00:48:02.000 --> 00:48:04.000
Cor, blimey!

644
00:48:04.000 --> 00:48:08.000
One of England's most famous
myths has become a reality

645
00:48:08.000 --> 00:48:10.000
as a new king has been crowned.

646
00:48:10.000 --> 00:48:14.000
Bob, who appears to be
a bald, jaundiced child,

647
00:48:14.000 --> 00:48:16.000
has pulled the famed sword
right from its stone,

648
00:48:16.000 --> 00:48:19.000
which, legend dictates,
makes him the new king.

649
00:48:19.000 --> 00:48:23.000
Tiny yellow traitor!

650
00:48:36.000 --> 00:48:38.000
England!

651
00:48:38.000 --> 00:48:40.000
England! England!

652
00:48:40.000 --> 00:48:42.000
England!
England! England!

653
00:48:42.000 --> 00:48:46.000
England! England...

654
00:48:51.000 --> 00:48:54.000
Ha, ha!

655
00:49:12.000 --> 00:49:15.000
Bello!

656
00:49:15.000 --> 00:49:17.000
Cut!

657
00:49:27.000 --> 00:49:31.000
Hey, Bob.

658
00:49:37.000 --> 00:49:39.000
- Hello, King Bob.
- Uh...

659
00:49:39.000 --> 00:49:42.000
Welcome to Buckingham Palace.

660
00:49:42.000 --> 00:49:43.000
Uh, no.

661
00:49:43.000 --> 00:49:46.000
Oh, what's the matter,
Your Majesty?

662
00:49:46.000 --> 00:49:48.000
Whatever's bothering you,
we can make it right.

663
00:49:48.000 --> 00:49:49.000
Just name it!

664
00:49:49.000 --> 00:49:51.000
Oh.

665
00:49:51.000 --> 00:49:54.000
Buddies!

666
00:49:54.000 --> 00:49:57.000
Buddies! Buddies!

667
00:49:58.000 --> 00:50:01.000
Buddies!

668
00:50:03.000 --> 00:50:05.000
Oh.

669
00:50:13.000 --> 00:50:16.000
Uh...

670
00:50:18.000 --> 00:50:21.000
King Bob!

671
00:50:21.000 --> 00:50:22.000
Long live the king!

672
00:50:22.000 --> 00:50:25.000
King Bob!

673
00:50:29.000 --> 00:50:32.000
...Bob...
...King...

674
00:50:44.000 --> 00:50:47.000
So...

675
00:51:01.000 --> 00:51:03.000
King Bob!

676
00:51:10.000 --> 00:51:13.000
Oh... Yeah!

677
00:51:13.000 --> 00:51:16.000
King Bob! Wait!

678
00:51:16.000 --> 00:51:19.000
- Wow!
- Whoa!

679
00:51:20.000 --> 00:51:22.000
Whoo-hoo!

680
00:51:24.000 --> 00:51:25.000
Oh...

681
00:51:25.000 --> 00:51:26.000
Yee-haw!

682
00:51:26.000 --> 00:51:27.000
King Bob!

683
00:51:27.000 --> 00:51:29.000
Hyah!

684
00:51:36.000 --> 00:51:39.000
Hmm? Huh! Ah!

685
00:51:45.000 --> 00:51:48.000
Yes, King Bob. Oh.

686
00:51:49.000 --> 00:51:53.000
King Bob?

687
00:51:53.000 --> 00:51:54.000
Ah, Claire.

688
00:51:54.000 --> 00:51:56.000
Mmm, Tiffany.

689
00:51:56.000 --> 00:51:59.000
Rawr!

690
00:52:04.000 --> 00:52:07.000
Ball!

691
00:52:07.000 --> 00:52:10.000
How dare you!

692
00:52:16.000 --> 00:52:17.000
Scarlet!

693
00:52:17.000 --> 00:52:21.000
Don't you "Scarlet" me,
you backstabbing little traitors!

694
00:52:21.000 --> 00:52:25.000
Using Herb's invention
to steal my crown?

695
00:52:26.000 --> 00:52:28.000
I feel used.
Not gonna lie.

696
00:52:28.000 --> 00:52:34.000
You stole my dream!
I was going to conquer England someday!

697
00:52:34.000 --> 00:52:36.000
There was gonna be a coronation,

698
00:52:36.000 --> 00:52:39.000
and I was going
to be made Queen.

699
00:52:39.000 --> 00:52:41.000
Every moment was planned.

700
00:52:41.000 --> 00:52:44.000
I'd wear a dress so sparkly,
it glowed!

701
00:52:44.000 --> 00:52:48.000
And everyone who ever
doubted me would be watching,

702
00:52:48.000 --> 00:52:51.000
and they would be crying!

703
00:52:51.000 --> 00:52:55.000
I was going to be
the picture of elegance and class!

704
00:52:55.000 --> 00:52:58.000
And you pinheads screwed it up!

705
00:52:58.000 --> 00:53:01.000
No, no, no!

706
00:53:02.000 --> 00:53:05.000
No, no, no, King Bob!
You cannot just abdicate the throne!

707
00:53:05.000 --> 00:53:07.000
Who invited the square?

708
00:53:07.000 --> 00:53:11.000
And you definitely cannot just
give the job to this woman!

709
00:53:11.000 --> 00:53:12.000
There are laws!

710
00:53:12.000 --> 00:53:15.000
Boss.
...Boss.

711
00:53:19.000 --> 00:53:21.000
...Scarlet Popapil!

712
00:53:21.000 --> 00:53:24.000
King Bob has officially changed the law,

713
00:53:24.000 --> 00:53:25.000
Clearing the way
for Scarlet Overkill

714
00:53:25.000 --> 00:53:27.000
to be crowned Queen of England!

715
00:53:27.000 --> 00:53:31.000
She will be coronated
at London's historic Westminster Abbey.

716
00:53:31.000 --> 00:53:35.000
If I wasn't so polite,
I'd say this spells certain doom for the country,

717
00:53:35.000 --> 00:53:36.000
if not the world.

718
00:53:36.000 --> 00:53:40.000
But I'm so very polite
that I shall keep my mouth shut.

719
00:53:40.000 --> 00:53:43.000
But, seriously,
we're all in big trouble.

720
00:53:43.000 --> 00:53:45.000
Scarlet! Scarlet!

721
00:53:45.000 --> 00:53:48.000
I don't have time
to answer any questions.

722
00:53:48.000 --> 00:53:50.000
I just want to
thank the Minions

723
00:53:50.000 --> 00:53:53.000
