to prepare for the coronation?

767
00:56:48.000 --> 00:56:51.000
Well, I hope you learned
your lesson for today.

768
00:56:52.000 --> 00:56:57.000
And by the way, it was me,
Herb, the whole time!

769
00:56:58.000 --> 00:57:01.000
I don't even know
anyone named "Blerb"!

770
00:57:01.000 --> 00:57:03.000
Uh, Herb...

771
00:57:03.000 --> 00:57:05.000
Oh. Huh.

772
00:57:05.000 --> 00:57:10.000
I am hours away from becoming
the Queen of England!

773
00:57:10.000 --> 00:57:12.000
I know!
It's a gas!

774
00:57:12.000 --> 00:57:14.000
I will finally get my crown.
Yeah.

775
00:57:14.000 --> 00:57:19.000
It's all I've ever wanted.
I'm going to be so happy.

776
00:57:19.000 --> 00:57:22.000
But let me ask you
something, Fabrice.

777
00:57:22.000 --> 00:57:26.000
Does that look like this to you?

778
00:57:27.000 --> 00:57:34.000
Mrs. Overkill,
the hair in that picture,
it's just two wavy lines!

779
00:57:34.000 --> 00:57:36.000
Oh, so, what,
now you're an art critic?

780
00:57:36.000 --> 00:57:41.000
I drew that when I was five years old!
Get out of my sight!

781
00:57:44.000 --> 00:57:46.000
Bye, Fabrice!

782
00:57:46.000 --> 00:57:49.000
I liked him. He was fun.

783
00:57:49.000 --> 00:57:51.000
So, what do you
think of the dress?

784
00:57:51.000 --> 00:57:57.000
Oh, it's so beautiful.
So fashion-forward.
So Valentino.

785
00:57:57.000 --> 00:58:00.000
Gave it a sweetheart
neckline because you're my sweetheart.

786
00:58:00.000 --> 00:58:02.000
The high collar
and cinched waist

787
00:58:02.000 --> 00:58:04.000
